answer.worked:
Region III is the area below $y=x^3$.
$$\begin{align*}
A_{\text{III}} &= \int_0^1 x^3\,dx \\
&= \left[\frac{x^4}{4}\right]_0^1 \\
&= \frac{1}{4}
\end{align*}$$
Region I is the area between $y=\sqrt{x}$ and $y=x^3$.
$$\begin{align*}
A_{\text{I}} &= \int_0^1 (\sqrt{x}-x^3)\,dx \\
&= \left[\frac{2}{3}x^{\frac{3}{2}}-\frac{x^4}{4}\right]_0^1 \\
&= \frac{2}{3}-\frac{1}{4} \\
&= \frac{5}{12}
\end{align*}$$
Region II is the remaining area in the unit square.
$$\begin{align*}
A_{\text{II}} &= 1-\frac{1}{4}-\frac{5}{12} \\
&= \frac{1}{3}
\end{align*}$$
The areas are $\dfrac{5}{12}$, $\dfrac{1}{3}$ and $\dfrac{1}{4}$ square units for regions I, II and III.

